WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.466
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:09.292
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:15.182
Unit one: To Be (am/is/are). Today you will talk about people and things with am, is and are.

4
00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.099
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.033 --> 00:00:22.197
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:23.691
Am.

7
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:27.031
Am means the form of be that we use with I.

8
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:28.931
I am a student.

9
00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:31.600
Your turn. Say: Am.

10
00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.119
Am.

11
00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:36.583
Is.

12
00:00:37.583 --> 00:00:40.906
Is means the form of be that we use with he, she and it.

13
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:42.645
She is happy.

14
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.368
Your turn. Say: Is.

15
00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:49.130
Is.

16
00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.699
Are.

17
00:00:51.683 --> 00:00:54.635
Are means the form of be that we use with you, we and they.

18
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.541
You are my friend.

19
00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:59.454
Your turn. Say: Are.

20
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.104
Are.

21
00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:04.642
I am.

22
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.230
I am means the short way to say who you are.

23
00:01:08.817 --> 00:01:10.352
I am from Cambodia.

24
00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:13.289
Your turn. Say: I am.

25
00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:17.146
I am.

26
00:01:17.883 --> 00:01:18.664
You are.

27
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.346
You are means we use it to talk to another person.

28
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.148
You are very kind.

29
00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.449
Your turn. Say: You are.

30
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.243
You are.

31
00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:32.926
He is.

32
00:01:33.917 --> 00:01:36.578
He is means we use it for one boy or man.

33
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:38.440
He is a teacher.

34
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:41.377
Your turn. Say: He is.

35
00:01:44.233 --> 00:01:45.142
He is.

36
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:46.687
She is.

37
00:01:47.683 --> 00:01:50.287
She is means we use it for one girl or woman.

38
00:01:50.883 --> 00:01:52.070
She is a doctor.

39
00:01:52.683 --> 00:01:55.080
Your turn. Say: She is.

40
00:01:57.933 --> 00:01:58.795
She is.

41
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:00.319
They are.

42
00:02:01.317 --> 00:02:04.199
They are means we use it for more than one person or thing.

43
00:02:04.783 --> 00:02:05.889
They are at school.

44
00:02:06.483 --> 00:02:09.170
Your turn. Say: They are.

45
00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:12.849
They are.

46
00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:17.203
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:23.015
Visal, how do we say who we are? We say 'I am Visal.' Why do we use 'am'?

48
00:02:24.117 --> 00:02:33.747
Because the verb be changes with the subject. We use am with I, is with he, she and it, and are with you, we and they.

49
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.687
Can you give me more examples?

50
00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:48.248
Yes! He is a teacher. She is happy. They are students. You are my friend. When we speak, we often say I'm, he's and they're.

51
00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:51.582
What about questions and negatives?

52
00:02:52.683 --> 00:03:01.074
For a question, put the verb first: Are you ready? For a negative, add not: I am not tired. She is not at home.

53
00:03:02.233 --> 00:03:04.128
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.888
Grammar focus: To be: am and is and are.

55
00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.445
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.418
I am a student.

57
00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:13.608
She is happy today.

58
00:03:14.517 --> 00:03:15.878
They are at school.

59
00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:23.387
Use am with I, is with he, she and it, and are with you, we and they. In questions, put the verb first.

60
00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.348
Be careful! Don't say: I is a student.

61
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.218
Say: I am a student.

62
00:03:31.518 --> 00:03:32.902
Use am with I.

63
00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.387
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:38.131
Who Is Who?.

65
00:03:38.431 --> 00:03:41.673
I am a student at C2 E P E Digital Academy.

66
00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:45.270
My teacher is kind, and she is very funny.

67
00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:48.336
My friends are in the same class.

68
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:51.704
You are my friend too, and we are a good team.

69
00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:55.245
He is my brother, and they are my parents.

70
00:03:56.333 --> 00:04:00.567
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:02.940
I blank ten years old.

72
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.255
A, am. B, is. C, are.

73
00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.440
The answer is A: am.

74
00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:14.188
She blank my teacher.

75
00:04:14.488 --> 00:04:17.329
A, are. B, am. C, is.

76
00:04:20.867 --> 00:04:22.727
The answer is C: is.

77
00:04:23.883 --> 00:04:25.151
They blank at school.

78
00:04:25.451 --> 00:04:28.234
A, is. B, are. C, am.

79
00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:33.916
The answer is B: are.

80
00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.783
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:37.083 --> 00:04:41.618
A, He are happy.. B, He is happy.. C, He am happy..

82
00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.549
The answer is B: He is happy..

83
00:04:48.683 --> 00:04:51.170
According to the reading, who is very funny?

84
00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:55.495
A, my teacher. B, my brother. C, my parents.

85
00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:01.207
The answer is A: my teacher.

86
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.610
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:09.785
Write one sentence using 'am', one using 'is', and one using 'are'.

88
00:05:18.583 --> 00:05:20.060
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:32.132
I am a student. My sister is a teacher. We are at home today. I use am with I, is with one person like my sister, and are with more than one person or with we, you and they.

90
00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.897
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:34.783 --> 00:05:39.200
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and to be: am and is and are.

92
00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.756
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

93
00:05:43.056 --> 00:05:45.535
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

94
00:05:45.835 --> 00:05:49.230
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

